Adam Lawson wrote:

> And yeah, Diablo isn't a shooter of any sort. Douglas may have been
> thinking of the Heretic/Hexen games, which are medieval-ish and first-
> person. Diablo isn't first person at all, the view is similar to the
> Zelda games. It's kind of like someone made a real-time graphical nethack
> clone (after taking out half the content).

True, Diablo in fact *is* Rogue-like game, like Nethack, it just don't
utilize ASCII-graphics. In fact, it was started to develope as a
turn-based game, but during developement it was transformed into
real-time game. However you can still see the affect of turns in the
gameplay.

I wouldn't be so quick to label Diablo having "only" half the content
of Nethack. For example skills (and more important, skill combinations)
and massive amount of items, make it in some ways much more versatile
as NH is.

What it lacks compared to Nethack is certain feel of "realism". It is
just more straightforward kill'em all -type game, and the monsters are
more limited to destructive behaviour.

I don't see any reason why somebody couldn't like them both.



